{
  "question_num": 4,
  "total_marks": 13,
  "title": "Progressive and stationary sound waves",
  "main_stem": null,
  "parts": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "For a progressive wave, state what is meant by the frequency.",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)",
      "part_stem": "A loudspeaker, microphone and cathode-ray oscilloscope (CRO) are arranged as shown in Fig. 4.1.\n\nFig. 4.1\n\nThe loudspeaker is emitting a sound wave which is detected by the microphone and displayed on the screen of the CRO as shown in Fig. 4.2.\n\nFig. 4.2\n\nThe time-base on the CRO is set to $0.50\\,\\text{ms}\\,\\text{cm}^{-1}$ and the $y$-gain is set to $0.20\\,\\text{V}\\,\\text{cm}^{-1}$.\n\nCalculate:",
      "text": "the frequency of the sound wave",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": "Hz"
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "the amplitude of the signal received by the CRO.",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": "V"
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "The intensity of the sound wave in (b) is reduced to a quarter of its original intensity without a change in frequency. Assume that the amplitude of the signal received by the CRO is proportional to the amplitude of the sound wave.\n\nOn Fig. 4.2, sketch the trace that is now seen on the screen of the CRO.",
      "marks": 3,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(d)",
      "part_stem": "A metal sheet is now placed in front of the loudspeaker in (b), as shown in Fig. 4.3.\n\nFig. 4.3\n\nA stationary wave is formed between the loudspeaker and the metal sheet.",
      "text": "State the principle of superposition.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(d)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "The initial position of the microphone is such that the trace on the CRO has an amplitude minimum. It is now moved a distance of $1.05\\,\\text{m}$ away from the loudspeaker along the line joining the loudspeaker and metal sheet.\n\nAs the microphone moves, it passes through three positions where the trace has an amplitude maximum before ending at a position where the trace has an amplitude minimum.\n\nDetermine the wavelength of the sound wave.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": "m"
    },
    {
      "label": "(d)(iii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Use your answers in (b)(i) and (d)(ii) to determine the speed of the sound in the air.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": "m s^{-1}"
    }
  ],
  "markscheme": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "number of crests / troughs / oscillations / waves passing a fixed point per unit time or number of oscillations per unit time of source / point on wave / particle of medium"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "period $T = 4.0 \\times 0.50\\,\\text{ms} = 2.0\\,\\text{ms}$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "frequency $f = 1/T = 500\\,\\text{Hz}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "amplitude $= 2.8 \\times 0.20 = 0.56\\,\\text{V}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)",
      "marks": 3,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "same frequency / period / number of waves trace"
        },
        {
          "tag": "M1",
          "text": "constant amplitude less than $2.8\\,\\text{cm}$ throughout"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "amplitude halved, $1.4\\,\\text{cm}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(d)(i)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "when two or more waves meet (at a point)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "the resultant displacement is the sum of the individual displacements"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(d)(ii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$1.05\\,\\text{m}$ is 3 node-to-node separations / $1.05 = 3\\lambda/2$ where node-to-node separation is $\\lambda/2$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "wavelength $\\lambda = 0.70\\,\\text{m}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(d)(iii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$v = f\\lambda$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$v = 350\\,\\text{m}\\,\\text{s}^{-1}$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
